{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner on jam room note revision 8 (0861580e, invitation b8b45b93): the added clause stands as written. An entry's effect bar is never before the effect bar of the entry before it in sequence. The room has one sequence, so one monotone rule keeps every change in entry order after a lookahead is lowered; the per-instrument form would need a tie rule across instruments for tempo and rules changes and is not wanted. The cost, a delay of an unrelated instrument's pattern in the rare case of a lowered lookahead, is accepted. On contract revision 23 (after 675776bc): the checker's qualification is right and stays in the text; the index is the owner's requirement for a bounded and replayable selection, not a claim that the scan was unbounded."}